from pathlib import Path
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];s=(r/'wacv2007-v5.tex').read_text()
s=s.replace('encoder training and probe fitting','encoder training and label-classifier fitting')
s=s.replace('the full-budget experiment described in the capstone notebook','the primary notebook-defined experiment')
s=s.replace('a visibility value for each sampled frame.', 'a visibility value for each sampled frame. Visibility is the detector\'s estimate of whether a landmark is visible; it is neither a clinical confidence score nor an independently measured quality rating.')
s=s.replace('If source $s$ contributes $n_s$ clips, each clip receives weight $1/n_s$.', 'For example, each of the 13 clips from one MS source contributes weight $1/13$, while a clip from a source with only one clip contributes weight one. More generally, if source $s$ contributes $n_s$ clips, each clip receives weight $1/n_s$.')
s=s.replace('Class balancing in the linear head does not make its training loss source-balanced.', 'These class weights do not equalize recordings within a label: a source with many clips still has more influence on classifier fitting than a source with one clip.')
s=s.replace('The target encoder receives the complete, untransformed window without a loss gradient.', 'The target encoder receives the complete, untransformed window and changes only through weight averaging.')
s=s.replace('With predicted features $u$, target features $z$, and running center $c$, the distributions are $p=\\operatorname{softmax}(u/0.10)$ and $q=\\operatorname{softmax}((z-c)/0.06)$. Cross-entropy is averaged over masked tokens within each example and then over examples. Once per batch, the center retains 90\\% of its previous value and adds 10\\% of the masked teacher-feature mean. This center is token-weighted, whereas the loss weights examples equally after their within-example averages. EMA momentum follows a cosine schedule from 0.996 toward one.', 'Training penalizes disagreement between predicted and reference features. Each 96-number vector is converted to nonnegative weights that sum to one, and cross-entropy measures how closely the two distributions agree. A running mean centers the reference features before this conversion; the temperature settings in Table~\\ref{tab:settings} control how concentrated the distributions become. We first average the error over hidden positions within a window, then give each window equal weight in its batch. The running mean is updated once per batch from all masked reference vectors, so this centering step weights token positions equally. The exact equations and update rules appear in the companion methods record.')
s=s.replace('This gives five outer evaluations with one inner holdout each, rather than an exhaustive nested search.', 'This gives five test evaluations, each with one validation group; we do not search across every possible inner split.')
s=s.replace('Within label strata', 'Within label groups').replace('within label strata','within each label group')
s=s.replace('Continuation lowers the final sampled training-minibatch loss in every fold, yet its validation score improves in only two. This shows a mismatch between those optimization summaries and stage selection; it does not compare the expected losses of both stages on a common evaluation set.', 'The final training batch has lower prediction error after continuation in every fold, yet the validation classification score improves in only two. Lower error on that sampled batch therefore did not reliably identify the stage selected for classification. Because the endpoint batches differ, these values do not measure average prediction error on a common evaluation set.')
s=s.replace('Mean pose is a demanding control here because it retains body configuration while discarding frame order.', 'Mean pose retains average body configuration and can reflect time spent in different positions, even though it discards their order. Its competitiveness therefore does not imply that all movement-related information has been removed.')
(r/'wacv2007-v6.tex').write_text(s)
(r/'evidence/method-details.md').write_text(r'''# Technical method details accompanying the readable manuscript

The top-level notebooks define this experiment; `notebook-audit.md` maps the details to cells and implementation. These equations restate the evaluated training procedure, rather than describing a new run.

For predicted feature vector u, reference vector z, and running center c, p = softmax(u / 0.10) and q = softmax((z - c) / 0.06). For each training window, average -sum_d q_d log(p_d) over its target token positions; average those per-window losses equally across the batch. The reference encoder does not receive loss gradients. Once per batch, update c to 0.9 c + 0.1 times the mean of all masked reference vectors. The center therefore weights target positions equally, whereas the final loss weights windows equally. The reference encoder is an exponential moving average of the context encoder, with cosine momentum from .996 toward1 over each stage.

Training uses the exact architecture and settings shown in the manuscript's settings table. The stochastic masks, distinct feature readout mask, geometric transforms, source-uniform window sampling, and restarted continuation state are documented in `notebook-audit.md`. Stage2 preserves network weights but starts a new optimizer, center, schedules and seeded sampling streams; it is not one uninterrupted1200-update call.

The exact source split is shuffled `StratifiedKFold` applied to one row for each sorted unique source. Five outer folds use seed42. Within the outer development set, the first of four stratified splits with seed43+k forms validation. The registry in `reproducibility.md` fixes membership. Scaling and label-classifier fitting use training clips only, and validation selects between the two trained stages before test feature extraction.

The recorded frame rate15 is the requested extraction target, not a retained per-clip elapsed-time guarantee. Coordinates are converted from MediaPipe image fractions to pixels, cleaned and interpolated, then centered on the hip midpoint and divided by torso length for the encoder and mean-pose control. See `claim-ledger.md` for the distinct cached-coordinate branches and their limits.

The original reference list was fully checked for bibliographic identity in `reference-audit.md`; retained claim support is mapped in `venue-and-literature.md`. No new disease mechanism, patient identity, diagnostic label, or permission fact is supplied by these technical details.
'''.replace('toward1','toward 1').replace('Stage2','Stage 2').replace('uninterrupted1200','uninterrupted 1,200').replace('seed42','seed 42').replace('seed43+k','seed 43+k').replace('rate15','rate 15'))
